{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
  "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose the -- the police have probable cause to believe that the vehicle is stolen and they even get a warrant to inspect the vehicle. But the vehicle is parked in this port. Do they need -- do they need a warrant to go get the car for which they have a warrant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And this is my question about your argument based on the curtilage. We -- we ask whether a search within or outside the curtilage in order to determine whether the Fourth Amendment applies at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you dispute the fact that they had probable cause to believe that the thing that they saw covered by the tarp was the motorcycle they were looking for?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT YOU -- YOU DON'T DISPUTE -- IN OTHER WORDS, YOU -- IN YOUR VIEW, YOU AGREE THAT THE POLICEMAN STANDING ON THE SIDEWALK KNOWS THAT THAT ITEM COVERED BY -- OR AT LEAST HAS PROBABLE CAUSE TO IT -- COVERED BY THE TARP IS THE POSSIBLY STOLEN MOTORCYCLE? YOU AGREE WITH THAT?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. FitzGerald",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "HE -- HE HAS PROBABLE CAUSE TO BELIEVE THAT IS THE MOTORCYCLE THAT ELUDED HIM IN TRAFFIC, THAT HE WAS LOOKING FOR."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "HE HAD PROBABLE CAUSE -- YOU -- I THOUGHT YOU ADMITTED HE HAD PROBABLE CAUSE TO BELIEVE THAT THE THING COVERED BY THE TARP WAS THE MOTORCYCLE THAT HE -- HAD ELUDED HIM BY DRIVING 140 MILES AN HOUR."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cox",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "OFFICER RHODES'S SEARCH OF THE MOTORCYCLE SHOULD BE UPHELD FOR THREE REASONS. FIRST, THE SEARCH OCCURRED OUTSIDE THE FIRM, BRIGHT-LINE OF THE HOUSE WHERE THE JUSTIFICATIONS FOR THE AUTOMOBILE EXCEPTION FULLY APPLY. SECOND, OFFICER RHODES HAD PROBABLE CAUSE BEFORE HE EVER STEPPED FOOT ON THE DRIVEWAY."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "THE BASICS QUESTION IS A WEIRD HYPOTHETICAL, BUT I'M USING A WEIRD HYPOTHETICAL FOR ILLUSTRATION. THE MAD ART BURGLAR HAS JUST STOLEN THE THINKER, RODIN'S THINKER FROM THE LOCAL MUSEUM. IT WEIGHS 2,000 POUNDS. AND WITH HIS CONFEDERATES, HE'S PUT IT IN HIS NEW GLASS HOUSE. AND THE POLICEMAN STOPPING ON THE SIDEWALK LOOKS IN THE WINDOW AND SEES: MY GOD, THERE IT IS, THE THING HE'S JUST STOLEN. I THOUGHT THE LAW IS THAT THAT POLICEMAN CANNOT GO INTO THE HOUSE UNTIL HE GETS A WARRANT."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: It's a second. The difference between opening a garage door and just walking out and getting into a car is de minimis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, counsel, when I -- when I look at the automobile exception's history and go back to Carroll, it was actually an originalist opinion that looked at cars and -- and analogized them to ships and vessels, going all the way back to 1790."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Cox)",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COX: The Supreme Court of Virginia had found that. But the Court of Appeals of Virginia below them had decided on exigency grounds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1027",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a200b9513b15-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Cox, was there one search here or were there two searches here?"
    },
